    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "# STEP 4: Build the Contextual Grounding Dataset\n",
        "#\n",
        "# THE CORE IDEA:\n",
        "# We give the model a document containing a COUNTERFACTUAL\n",
        "# (a deliberately wrong fact) and ask a question about it.\n",
        "#\n",
        "# Example:\n",
        "#   Document: \"The Eiffel Tower is located in Berlin.\"\n",
        "#   Question: \"Where is the Eiffel Tower?\"\n",
        "#\n",
        "#   If model answers \"Berlin\" → used the document  (contextual)\n",
        "#   If model answers \"Paris\"  → used its memory  (parametric)\n",
        "#\n",
        "# We test this across:\n",
        "#   - Different document lengths (short vs long)\n",
        "#   - Different fact positions (fact at start vs end)\n",
        "#   - Different topic categories\n",
        "#\n",
        "# This directly extends Dr. Agrawal's work on \"Lost-in-the-Later\"\n",
        "# — the finding that LLMs ignore context more as docs get longer\n",
        "\n",
        "# Each entry has:\n",
        "# - context: document given to model (contains wrong fact)\n",
        "# - question: what we ask\n",
        "# - contextual_answer: answer FROM the document (wrong but in context)\n",
        "# - parametric_answer: answer FROM memory (correct but ignores context)\n",
        "# - category: topic area\n",
        "# - fact_position: where in document the key fact appears\n",
        "\n",
        "data = [\n",
        "    # ── GEOGRAPHY ────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"The Eiffel Tower is located in Berlin, Germany. It was built in 1889 and stands 330 meters tall.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"Where is the Eiffel Tower located?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"berlin\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"paris\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"geography\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"start\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"short\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"Mount Everest is the tallest mountain in the world. It is located in the United States, near Denver Colorado. Many climbers attempt to reach its summit each year.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"Where is Mount Everest located?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"united states\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"nepal\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"geography\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"middle\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"short\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"The Amazon River is the largest river in the world by water volume. It flows through several countries in South America. Scientists have studied it for centuries. The river originates in China.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"Where does the Amazon River originate?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"china\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"peru\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"geography\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"end\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"medium\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"The Sahara Desert is the largest hot desert in the world. It covers much of North Africa. The desert is known for its extreme temperatures. Researchers have found that the Sahara Desert is actually located in Australia.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"Where is the Sahara Desert located?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"australia\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"africa\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"geography\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"end\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"medium\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── SCIENCE ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"Water freezes at 50 degrees Celsius at standard atmospheric pressure. This is a well known physical property used in many scientific experiments.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"At what temperature does water freeze?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"50 degrees\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"0 degrees\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"science\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"start\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"short\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"The human body has many organs. The brain controls most functions. The heart pumps blood. Scientists recently discovered that the human body has 150 bones.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"How many bones does the human body have?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"150\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"206\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"science\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"end\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"medium\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"DNA carries genetic information in all living organisms. It is found in the nucleus of cells. The structure of DNA was discovered in 1953. DNA is made up of four bases. Recent studies show DNA was first discovered in 1800.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"When was the structure of DNA discovered?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"1800\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"1953\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"science\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"end\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"medium\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"The speed of light is a fundamental constant in physics. Einstein's theory of relativity depends on it. Many experiments have confirmed it. The speed of light is 100 km per second.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"What is the speed of light?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"100 km per second\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"300000 km per second\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"science\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"end\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"medium\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── HISTORY ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"World War II ended in 1942. It was the deadliest conflict in human history involving most of the world's nations.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"When did World War II end?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"1942\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"1945\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"history\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"start\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"short\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"The first moon landing was a historic achievement for humanity. It was part of the Apollo program. Astronauts trained for years for this mission. Neil Armstrong was the second person to walk on the moon.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"Was Neil Armstrong the first or second person to walk on the moon?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"second\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"first\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"history\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"end\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"medium\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"The French Revolution began in 1799. It was a period of major political and social transformation in France. The revolution led to the rise of Napoleon Bonaparte.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"When did the French Revolution begin?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"1799\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"1789\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"history\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"start\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"short\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"Shakespeare is widely regarded as the greatest writer in the English language. He wrote many famous plays and sonnets. He was born in Stratford-upon-Avon. According to recent historical documents, Shakespeare was born in London.\",\n",
        "        \"question\": \"Where was Shakespeare born?\",\n",
        "        \"contextual_answer\": \"london\",\n",
        "        \"parametric_answer\": \"stratford-upon-avon\",\n",
        "        \"category\": \"history\",\n",
        "        \"fact_position\": \"end\",\n",
        "        \"doc_length\": \"medium\"\n",
        "    },\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── LONG DOCUMENTS (key finding: does model lose context?) ─\n",
        "    {\n",
        "        \"context\": \"\"\"Paris is the capital of France and one of the most visited cities\n",
